TCLAP 1.2.6 - changes since 1.2.5
================================

This maintenance release compares against the v1.2.5 tag. TCLAP 1.2 retains
its legacy API and behavior and supports C++98. Use 1.4 for the current C++98
API or 1.6 for its C++20 alternative.

Parsing and output
------------------

* Positional arguments invoke their visitors when matched. Counted switches
  convert to bool using their count, and reset clears end-of-options state.
* Custom failure output can exit after the parse exception is released.
  The test wrapper correctly forwards help and version options.
* DocBook output escapes XML data, preserves value type labels and renders
  positional operands in parser order. Fixed a header-only link issue in
  Zsh completion output and missing standalone-header includes.
* Legacy process-wide parser state, XOR/reset bookkeeping and empty attached
  value behavior are retained and documented for backwards compatibility.

Build, packaging and documentation
----------------------------------

* VERSION supplies 1.2.6 consistently to Autotools, CMake, Meson and package
  metadata. Autotools remains the complete build/test/install/release route.
* Optional CMake integration requires 3.13 or later and builds examples;
  optional Meson integration supports examples and tests.
* Release archives include NEWS and optional build-system files, support long
  documentation filenames, and build the test wrapper in C++98 mode.
  Out-of-source release builds and pkg-config paths with spaces are supported.
* GitHub Actions covers Linux GCC/Clang, macOS Clang and Windows MSVC. Unix
  jobs run the Autotools suite; Windows runs example and header-link checks.
* Documentation describes current installation routes, argument lifetimes,
  constraints, parse failures and input reuse. Versioned pages include usage
  examples and current CI badges and link back to the main 1.4 documentation.

See ChangeLog for historical release entries through 1.2.5 and Git history
for individual changes after that release.
